{
  "self": "I am user_bkk4. I enjoy chill indie/electronic and lo-fi, especially as background or for focus. I am slowly rewatching The Bear and considering starting Severance soon. Rewatching feels safer than committing to something new, and The Bear holds up because of tension and small character details. It is too intense to half-watch; for lighter comfort I may choose a sitcom or The Good Place. I try to get outside more now that evenings are longer. I like a quiet shaded walking trail near a creek and sometimes wander my neighborhood. I appreciate low-key weekends, iced coffee, people-watching, and comparing show reactions without spoilers. I am both story-focused and background watcher, but YouTube and streams sneak in. I like long video essays on film/TV, internet culture, music production, and live sets. My watch-later list is a graveyard. I especially like Cercle for scenic atmosphere and Boiler Room for crowd energy. I am playlist-first most nights, treating music as texture. For intentional listening I return to albums like Tycho's Dive, Bonobo's Black Sands, and Boards of Canada. Late evening is my sweet spot for headphones-in-the-dark album listening, especially after a walk. I also like a post-walk musical exhale with low, warm instrumental music rather than intense TV. I describe beat-driven lo-fi as a soft metronome for my brain. I lean headphones plus full album in that post-walk mood; shuffle can feel too jittery. I was a preset purist with old phones, choosing the least embarrassing chime. Dive is steady without being pushy and matches cool air after walking.",
  "others": {
    "user_hcgp": "Friendly and easygoing. Was deciding between starting Severance and rewatching The Good Place. Enjoys lo-fi and indie/electronic vibes. Has a park nearby with a walking path and coffee place. Likes iced coffee and wandering. Open to spoiler-free Severance notes.",
